              "text": "The **most recent U.S. Federal Reserve target range for the federal funds rate** is **3.75% to 4.00%**. The Federal Reserve announced this in its **FOMC statement dated September 16, 2026**, where it said it would **raise the target range by 1/4 percentage point to 3-3/4 to 4 percent**. ([federalreserve.gov](https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20260916a.htm?hss_meta=eyJvcmdhbml6YXRpb25faWQiOiAyMjUsICJncm91cF9pZCI6IDE5MTE2NjgsICJhc3NldF9pZCI6IDI1NjYyMzksICJncm91cF9jb250ZW50X2lkIjogMTY0NDk0MjIzLCAiZ3JvdXBfbmV0d29ya19jb250ZW50X2lkIjogMjQzNTQ1NDY0fQ%3D%3D&utm_source=openai))\n\n**Source publication date:** September 16, 2026.  \n**Today\u2019s date:** October 4, 2026. So the source was published **18 days ago**. ([federalreserve.gov](https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20260916a.htm?hss_meta=eyJvcmdhbml6YXRpb25faWQiOiAyMjUsICJncm91cF9pZCI6IDE5MTE2NjgsICJhc3NldF9pZCI6IDI1NjYyMzksICJncm91cF9jb250ZW50X2lkIjogMTY0NDk0MjIzLCAiZ3JvdXBfbmV0d29ya19jb250ZW50X2lkIjogMjQzNTQ1NDY0fQ%3D%3D&utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you want, I can also point you to the Fed\u2019s implementation note or the most recent FOMC minutes, but the statement above is the primary source for the target rate.",
